        text: `The Palace of Justice siege was a very violent event in Bogotá, Colombia, in 1985. A rebel group called M-19 took over the large building where the highest judges in the country worked. They took more than 300 people hostage. The Colombian army reacted very quickly and with a lot of power. They sent tanks and hundreds of soldiers to attack the building immediately. A massive battle started in the center of the city and a huge fire destroyed the building. The fighting lasted for two days. In the end, more than 100 people died, including many of the most important judges in Colombia. People were very sad because so many innocent lives were lost in the fire and the shooting. Many people criticized the army for using too much force instead of trying to talk to the rebels to save the hostages first. It is remembered as a very tragic day.`,
